      "comment": "MAGIC MONEY (7) brings the most persuasive recent form, with a second at Pakenham Synthetic over 1200m when beaten just under a length after racing close enough and being pipped late. His Ballarat Synthetic fourth in BM56 company two back also had merit, and the weight relief helps offset the first look at 1000m and the switch of state. SANCTIONS (9) resumes after three months and has enough profile to be a genuine danger, having placed two of three this season and shown a reliable record on good tracks despite still searching for a win around this trip. CASINO ROYALE (3) is the solid race-fit option, with consecutive thirds and a prior win at around 1000m, so he appeals as the runner most likely to hold his form. INTOXICATING (2) has to rebound from a plain last-start seventh, but her Mingenew second two runs ago keeps her in the mix for a minor share if she sharpens back up. POWER TO RULE (4) won't be far away.",
